  /// The replication type. When the replication type is full-load or
  /// full-load-and-cdc , the only valid value for the first run of the
  /// replication is start-replication . This option will start the
  /// replication. You can also use ReloadTables to reload specific tables
  /// that failed during replication instead of restarting the replication.
  /// The resume-processing option isn't applicable for a full-load
  /// replication, because you can't resume partially loaded tables during the
  /// full load phase. For a full-load-and-cdc replication, DMS migrates table
  /// data, and then applies data changes that occur on the source. To load
  /// all the tables again, and start capturing source changes, use
  /// reload-target . Otherwise use resume-processing , to replicate the
  /// changes from the last stop position.
  pub start_replication_type: Str? = None
  /// User-defined settings for the premigration assessment. The possible
  /// values are: ResultLocationFolder : The folder within an Amazon S3 bucket
  /// where you want DMS to store the results of this assessment run.
